# ADIF: a generic DATA mode is exported as MODE RTTY (NY4I 2026-10-23); and a received grid that lies in exactly one state of the call's country writes STATE and DXCC (NY4I 2026-11-25)
#
# 'DATA' is not an ADIF mode (rickmurphy.net's validator rejected NY4I's CQ WW
# SSB export). ADIF has no generic data mode, so -- NY4I's ruling, as issue
# 457 already did for Digital with no submode -- such a QSO is written as
# MODE RTTY, with <APP_TR4W_MODE_ASSUMED:1>Y so TR4W's own import restores the
# unknown data mode, and one free-text header line before the first tag
# counting them. ref.adi is D7-written and NEVER regenerated, so the records
# and the header line are pinned here as the exact expected difference.
#
# Read by run-golden-diff.sh AND test-adif-roundtrip.sh through known-pin-lib.sh: the lines
# below the comments are EXACTLY the changed lines of ref.adi vs the candidate.
#
# NY4I, 2026-11-24 (option A): a QSO that has a band but no frequency now writes the
# band's default FREQ (the Band Plan table, by band and mode) and
# <APP_TR4W_FREQ_ASSUMED:1>Y, so the record is deliverable to WRL and other
# loggers; the stored QSO keeps frequency 0 and TR4W's own import restores it.
# The D7 reference lacks FREQ on those QSOs and is never regenerated, so the
# changed records are pinned here as the exact expected difference.
#
# 2026-11-25 (NY4I: 'if we can determine the state from the actual grid sent, it
# seems reasonable to set the state'): a QSO that received a Maidenhead grid has
# STATE and DXCC written when the grid (uGridLookup, from the ARRL's vuccgrids.dat)
# reaches exactly ONE subdivision of the CALL'S OWN DXCC entity. An ambiguous grid
# (two states) or a call of another country gets none. The D7 reference wrote no
# STATE for these QSOs and is never regenerated, so the changed records are pinned
# here as the exact expected difference; KE0UI DM78, KE0NRE DM79, N6NXV CM87 and
# WB9RCE EN51 gain it, and the other grids in this log are ambiguous or unknown.
